<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdul Razak Hussein</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1922–1976</span> · Also known as Tun Abdul Razak</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdul Razak Hussein, known as Tun Abdul Razak, was the second prime minister of Malaysia, from 1970 until his death in 1976. After the race riots of 13 May 1969 he headed the National Operations Council that governed during the emergency, then launched the New Economic Policy and formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barisan-nasional">Barisan Nasional</a> coalition. He established relations with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in 1974, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najib-razak">Najib Razak</a> later became prime minister.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abdul-razak-hussein.jpg" alt="Abdul Razak Hussein" width="320" height="416" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Malaysian Government · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tun_Abdul_Razak_Official_Portrait_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
